\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces FreeReg overall architecture (network-style 3D block diagram). Note that FreeReg is a \emph  {geometric/optimization} pipeline rather than a learned neural network; the diagram uses a network-style layered-block rendering for clarity, and the correspondence front end is interface-isomorphic with (and swappable to) a learned network (e.g., FoundationPose). A 3D model (CT/CAD mesh) and an image/video stream (RGB-D or monocular) are fused by a multi-source correspondence engine (texture SIFT, geometric FPFH, render-and-compare templates) with contour-gated arbitration to a rigid pose $(\mathbf  {R},\mathbf  {t})\in SE(3)$; a manifold SE(3) Kalman filter with innovation gating temporally regularizes the pose; an observability-guided RTW estimator recovers deformation within the spectral observable subspace $\mathbf  {V}_{r}$; and a co-anchored 3D Gaussian Splatting renderer produces the MR composite, whose photometric residual feeds back (dashed) as an online, label-free validation signal. A scene graph resolves multi-model occlusion.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{2}{4}{FreeReg overall architecture (network-style 3D block diagram). Note that FreeReg is a \emph {geometric/optimization} pipeline rather than a learned neural network; the diagram uses a network-style layered-block rendering for clarity, and the correspondence front end is interface-isomorphic with (and swappable to) a learned network (e.g., FoundationPose). A 3D model (CT/CAD mesh) and an image/video stream (RGB-D or monocular) are fused by a multi-source correspondence engine (texture SIFT, geometric FPFH, render-and-compare templates) with contour-gated arbitration to a rigid pose $(\mathbf {R},\mathbf {t})\in SE(3)$; a manifold SE(3) Kalman filter with innovation gating temporally regularizes the pose; an observability-guided RTW estimator recovers deformation within the spectral observable subspace $\mathbf {V}_{r}$; and a co-anchored 3D Gaussian Splatting renderer produces the MR composite, whose photometric residual feeds back (dashed) as an online, label-free validation signal. A scene graph resolves multi-model occlusion}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{eq:rtwobj}{{3}{4}{Observability-guided and hierarchical RTW}{equation.3}{}}
\newlabel{eq:jacobian}{{4}{4}{Observability-guided and hierarchical RTW}{equation.4}{}}
\newlabel{thm:rank}{{1}{4}{Rank deficiency of single-view registration}{equation.4}{}}
