\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Non-rigid deformation recovery on a tubular airway/colon analog, visualized as projected surface points. Rows increase the bend amplitude (20/35/50\,mm). The rigid baseline (blue) remains straight; the ground truth (orange) bends into an arc; RTW (green) recovers that bend within the observable subspace. At 35 and 50\,mm, RTW reaches 6.05 and 8.28\,mm recovery error, respectively, versus 6.20 and 8.57\,mm for the rigid baseline.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dent}{{3}{7}{Non-rigid deformation recovery on a tubular airway/colon analog, visualized as projected surface points. Rows increase the bend amplitude (20/35/50\,mm). The rigid baseline (blue) remains straight; the ground truth (orange) bends into an arc; RTW (green) recovers that bend within the observable subspace. At 35 and 50\,mm, RTW reaches 6.05 and 8.28\,mm recovery error, respectively, versus 6.20 and 8.57\,mm for the rigid baseline}{figure.3}{}}
